---
import Divider from './Divider.astro';
import Hero from './Hero.astro';
---
<Divider
  id="sec-6"
  section="VI · Our Portfolio"
  num="Section VI"
  title="Our Portfolio"
  bg="/impactreports/2025/ptf/images/farm-couto.jpg"
/>

<!-- Estate 1 -->
<Hero section="VI · Our Portfolio" bg="/impactreports/2025/ptf/images/farm-mariapires.jpg">
  <div class="kicker">Estate 01 of 02 · Alentejo</div>
  <h3 style="font-size:clamp(1.9rem,5vw,3rem);max-width:20ch;margin-top:0.4em">Herdade de Maria Pires &amp; Soberanas de Cima</h3>
  <p>Alvito &amp; Alcácer do Sal · the first properties acquired by the fund.</p>
</Hero>

<section class="section" data-section="VI · Our Portfolio">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split-page map reveal">
      <div class="col-text">
        <p>Located in Alentejo, straddling the municipalities of Alvito and Alcácer do Sal, these two properties were the first to be acquired by Pela Terra Farmland.</p>
        <p>The primary commercial crops grown are almonds and olives, planted in 2023. The first olives were harvested in 2025, with the first almond harvest planned in 2026.</p>
        <p>136 hectares, or 26 per cent of the total area of the properties, is primarily managed for biodiversity. This area mostly consists of cork and holm oak montado and wet grassland.</p>
        <p class="h-minor">A detailed baseline assessment carried out by NBI in 2023 identified:</p>
        <div class="statgrid" style="border:1px solid var(--line);grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin-top:0.6rem">
          <div class="cell"><div class="num">13</div><div class="lab">Different habitats</div></div>
          <div class="cell"><div class="num">126</div><div class="lab">Species of flora — 16 of conservation interest</div></div>
          <div class="cell"><div class="num">155</div><div class="lab">Fauna species — 22 of conservation interest</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="map-fig">
        <div class="img" style="background-image:url('/impactreports/2025/ptf/images/map-mariapires.jpg')"></div>
        <figcaption>NBI land-use map · Herdade de Maria Pires &amp; Soberanas de Cima</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Estate 2 -->
<Hero section="VI · Our Portfolio" light bg="/impactreports/2025/ptf/images/couto-orchard-2.jpg" bgStyle="opacity:0.55;right:0;left:auto;width:55%">
  <div class="kicker">Estate 02 of 02 · Centro</div>
  <h3 style="font-size:clamp(1.9rem,5vw,3rem);max-width:18ch;margin-top:0.4em">Couto das Ferrarias</h3>
  <p>Castelo Branco · acquired in 2024.</p>
</Hero>

<section class="section" data-section="VI · Our Portfolio">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split-page map reveal">
      <div class="col-text">
        <p>Located in the district of Castelo Branco, in the Centro region, Couto das Ferrarias was acquired by Pela Terra Farmland in 2024.</p>
        <p>The farm has a total area of 359 hectares, with super-intensive olive orchards covering 267 hectares.</p>
        <p>Around 39 hectares of the property (10.8 per cent of the total area) is made up of natural and semi-natural areas (grassland, scrubland, montado, wet grassland, and wet grassland with trees) and is primarily managed for biodiversity.</p>
        <p class="h-minor">A detailed baseline assessment carried out by NBI in 2024 identified:</p>
        <div class="statgrid" style="border:1px solid var(--line);grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin-top:0.6rem">
          <div class="cell"><div class="num">7</div><div class="lab">Different habitats</div></div>
          <div class="cell"><div class="num">131</div><div class="lab">Species of flora — 18 of conservation interest</div></div>
          <div class="cell"><div class="num">119</div><div class="lab">Fauna species — 13 of conservation interest</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="map-fig">
        <div class="img" style="background-image:url('/impactreports/2025/ptf/images/map-couto.jpg')"></div>
        <figcaption>NBI land-use map · Couto das Ferrarias</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
